From ba088e5ab1fb2b59d3237d88cf6d91021f0b4327 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:36:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] ga2: VU1 differential capture/replay harness;
 write-at-issue and other exact VU1 speedups

- GA2_VU1CAP=<file> samples VU1 execute/resume calls (GA2_VU1CAP_EVERY,
  GA2_VU1CAP_MAX) with their inputs and a digest of state, data memory,
  PATH1 bytes and cycles; ps2xTest/ga2_vu1_replay replays a capture through
  the current interpreter, reports mismatches and time per run.
- VF/VI/ACC results are written at issue: readers already stall until the
  ready cycle and the latest issued write wins, so this is identical to the
  delayed commit; only the latest ready cycle is kept so end-of-program
  flushes take the same time. Flags, Q/P and stores stay pipelined.
- XGKICK copies whole qwords and no longer clears its 64 KB buffer per kick.
- Decoded pairs are used by reference; MPG uploads of unchanged code no
  longer invalidate the decode cache.
- Replay of 10k captured runs (title, narration, movie, story): 0
  mismatches, 97 -> 71 us per run. Unit tests that inspected registers inside
  a budget-truncated run now rely on stall timing and final values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
